review:
Just wow.<br/><br/>You want to know what a movie with a story that doesn't make any sense, that contradict the movies before in the same franchise and make the main villain appear from nowhere and change his plan all the time in the same movie... Here you go you have it... This is what Rise of the Skywalker is an horrible movie with a it tone of action that go all over the place with tons of plots holes<br/><br/>What I like about this movie:<br/><br/>There is a lot of action so it's not as boring as episode 1 and 2;
I think that Rey being a Palpatine was a very good idea it just wasn't done right;
And prefer the way JJ use Luke a lot more than what RJ did with it. For the first time it really felt like we saw Luke from the original trilogy.<br/><br/>What I hate about this movie:
The fact that they bring back Palpatine without any explanation, it's just a terrible idea;
The overall story just doesn't make any sense and why Palpatine change his plan all the time? First he tell Kylo Ren that he want to give him a new empire but he have to kill Rey. After that when he meet Rey he tell her that he want her to take his place and he finally try to suck the life out of Ren and Rey to stay in charge. Wow we are far from the mastermind that manipulate Anakin in the prequel.
The way the use Lea character. They should just have make her dead in the beginning of the movie.
The teleportation force power. That is just stupid. Thank RJ to create this stupid force power and thank JJ to make it look like even stupider;<br/><br/>Seriously, I don't know what to say it's so awful and I'm amaze that some people actually like that garbage movie.
